func.func @main(%x: tensor<7x3xf32>) -> tensor<7x3xf32>

It must compute: out[i, j] = x[i, j] / sqrt(sum_k x[i, k]^2) (each row scaled to unit L2 norm).

Relevant operations: reduce, broadcast_in_dim, element-wise ops (add/subtract/multiply/divide/maximum/minimum/negate/exponential/sqrt/rsqrt/abs), constant.

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
func.func @main(%x: tensor<7x3xf32>) -> tensor<7x3xf32> {
  // Step 1: Square each element: x^2
  %x2 = stablehlo.multiply %x, %x : tensor<7x3xf32>

  // Step 2: Sum over axis 1 (columns) to get sum_k x[i, k]^2 for each row
  %zero = stablehlo.constant dense<0.0> : tensor<f32>
  %sum = "stablehlo.reduce"(%x2, %zero) ({
    ^bb0(%a: tensor<f32>, %b: tensor<f32>):
      %add = stablehlo.add %a, %b : tensor<f32>
      "stablehlo.return"(%add) : (tensor<f32>) -> ()
  }) {dimensions = array<i64: 1>} : (tensor<7x3xf32>, tensor<f32>) -> tensor<7xf32>

  // Step 3: Take sqrt of the sum to get L2 norm for each row
  %norm = stablehlo.sqrt %sum : tensor<7xf32>

  // Step 4: Broadcast norm to shape (7,3) for division
  %norm_bcast = "stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim"(%norm) {broadcast_dimensions = array<i64: 0>} : (tensor<7xf32>) -> tensor<7x3xf32>

  // Step 5: Divide x by norm_bcast
  %out = stablehlo.divide %x, %norm_bcast : tensor<7x3xf32>

  return %out : tensor<7x3xf32>
}
